---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Cookies | The Royal House of Engagement" description="How the Low Value Content website uses cookies and similar browser technologies.">
  <article class="plain-page">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Effective November 21, 2026</p><h1>Cookies.</h1><p>The storefront does not intentionally set advertising or analytics cookies.</p></header>
    <div class="rows">
    <section><h2>Current public site</h2><p>The cart saves product, variant, and quantity in your browser's local storage so it persists between visits. Hosting infrastructure may use necessary technical mechanisms to deliver and protect the service. No optional tracking technologies have been enabled.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Development and staging</h2><p>Restricted non-production environments use Google and Firebase for sign-in and session storage to remember an authorized email address during the browser session. Those environments are for internal review and are not the public storefront.</p></section>
    <section><h2>External services</h2><p>Stripe Checkout and any social platforms you visit may use their own cookies. Their notices and controls apply on those services.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Changes and controls</h2><p>If we add optional tracking, we will update this page and any required consent controls first. You can delete stored cart data through your browser settings. There is currently no optional Low Value Content cookie preference to manage.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
